      en: "Prats is a picturesque village within the parish of Canillo, situated on a sunny plateau overlooking the main valley. The village's architectural highlight is the Romanesque church of Sant Miquel de Prats, dating back to the late 11th or early 12th century. This church is noted for its simple design and a double-arched bell gable. Located near Prats are the enigmatic engravings of 'Roc de les Bruixes' (Witches' Rock), prehistoric rock carvings believed to date from the Bronze Age. The settlement has meticulously preserved its rural charm, featuring narrow alleys and historic stone dwellings. Due to its elevated strategic position, Prats offers expansive panoramic views of the Canillo valley and its surrounding peaks. Agriculture and livestock farming remain traditional staples of the community, shaping the local landscape. Prats is also a significant stop along the 'Camí Ral', the ancient royal road that historically connected the valleys of Andorra.",
